The kingdom of God invades the evil, right?

442
00:28:32,320 --> 00:28:39,700
He invades the unrighteousness and affects the people one at a time until they melt away and they receive the forgiveness that they can pass on to others.

443
00:28:39,700 --> 00:28:44,520
So it's a very clear picture that the kingdom of God wasn't there confronting.

444
00:28:44,520 --> 00:28:47,940
It wasn't there, but it was there challenging.

445
00:28:47,940 --> 00:28:50,040
He didn't say, would you please consider?

446
00:28:51,460 --> 00:28:54,300
It is a strong directive, you should repent.

447
00:28:54,300 --> 00:28:59,480
You will repent and believe in the gospel as a command, in the plural, to everyone listening, right?

448
00:28:59,480 --> 00:29:08,800
Luke 17, 20 through 21, the Pharisees now are asking Jesus, okay, you said the kingdom of God's here, where is it, right?

449
00:29:08,800 --> 00:29:13,540
The kingdom of God is not coming in ways that can be observed, Jesus answered.

450
00:29:13,540 --> 00:29:16,940
Nor will they say, look, here it is, or there.

451
00:29:16,940 --> 00:29:20,060
For behold, the kingdom of God is in the midst of you.

452
00:29:20,060 --> 00:29:27,640
Now the you there is a plural, and the word he used for in the midst of you, in some of your Bibles it will say among you or within you.

453
00:29:27,640 --> 00:29:37,120
The reason that it's translated oddly is because he's using a singular concept inside you and a plural object, right?

454
00:29:37,120 --> 00:29:39,280
It's inside all of you, right?

455
00:29:39,280 --> 00:29:40,640
It's among you.

456
00:29:40,640 --> 00:29:46,780
So the picture is that the kingdom of God comes into one person and fills an entire community.

457
00:29:47,300 --> 00:29:50,320
And it grows and spreads from person to person, right?

458
00:29:50,320 --> 00:29:53,520
John 18, 36.

459
00:29:53,520 --> 00:29:58,400
Pilate is now accosting Jesus.

460
00:29:58,400 --> 00:30:02,700
He's interrogating him, trying to understand if in fact he's a threat to the Roman Empire.

461
00:30:02,700 --> 00:30:06,620
He says, you know, what are you doing here?

462
00:30:06,620 --> 00:30:07,920
Jesus said, why?

463
00:30:07,920 --> 00:30:08,700
Who told you that?

464
00:30:08,700 --> 00:30:10,380
Or, you know, who told you that I was a king?

465
00:30:10,760 --> 00:30:13,260
And Pilate says, I'm not one of you horrible minorities.

466
00:30:13,260 --> 00:30:14,780
You shut up.

467
00:30:14,780 --> 00:30:17,340
You know, he's kind of rude to him and says, really, what have you done?

468
00:30:17,340 --> 00:30:17,960
Why are you here?

469
00:30:17,960 --> 00:30:22,780
And Jesus says in verse 36, my kingdom is not of this world.

470
00:30:22,780 --> 00:30:27,980
If my kingdom were of this world, my servants would have been fighting that I might not be delivered over to the Jews.

471
00:30:28,040 --> 00:30:29,820
But my kingdom is not from this world.

472
00:30:29,820 --> 00:30:37,900
So we see that the kingdom of God is not just coming and wiping off the planet the injustice.

473
00:30:39,000 --> 00:30:42,680
It's invading that injustice and inviting it to, and commanding it to repent.

474
00:30:42,680 --> 00:30:45,720
It is not visible.

475
00:30:45,720 --> 00:30:48,760
It invades the person and the community.

476
00:30:48,760 --> 00:30:51,560
And it's not political.

477
00:30:51,560 --> 00:30:55,040
It's not here to fight a political battle.

478
00:30:55,040 --> 00:31:01,660
It's not here as a part of any of the struggles we have against each other.

479
00:31:01,660 --> 00:31:04,200
It's here as a footprint from heaven, right?

480
00:31:04,200 --> 00:31:05,960
An outpost of the kingdom of heaven.

481
00:31:06,760 --> 00:31:09,180
So those are the three things Christ clearly says about it.

482
00:31:09,180 --> 00:31:14,440
In the letter of Colossians, which, again, was written at the same time as Ephesians,

483
00:31:14,440 --> 00:31:20,840
Paul has another statement or two that helps enlighten us, give us another perspective on Ephesians.

484
00:31:20,840 --> 00:31:24,540
He says, again, in Colossians 1, 9,

485
00:31:24,540 --> 00:31:29,220
I'm asking that you may be filled with knowledge of his will and all spiritual wisdom and understanding.

486
00:31:29,220 --> 00:31:33,200
Now, what did he say that he wanted to have wisdom and understanding of in Ephesians?

487
00:31:33,200 --> 00:31:35,680
The hope, the inheritance, and the power, right?

488
00:31:36,760 --> 00:31:44,080
And I want you to walk in a manner worthy of the Lord, fully pleasing him, bearing fruit in every good work and increasing in knowledge of God.

489
00:31:44,080 --> 00:31:45,460
What's that knowledge of God?

490
00:31:45,460 --> 00:31:48,040
The hope, the inheritance, and the power, right?

491
00:31:48,040 --> 00:31:53,000
I want to see you bearing fruit, being strengthened with all power, according to his glorious might.

492
00:31:53,080 --> 00:32:00,840
And for homework, if you want to go back and read through the bits of Ephesians and just note all the uses of glory and ask yourself what those are about, that'd be time well spent.

493
00:32:02,640 --> 00:32:08,000
He'll be strengthened with all that power, according to his glorious might, for all endurance and patience and joy.

494
00:32:08,000 --> 00:32:09,840
So, endurance and patience and joy.

495
00:32:09,840 --> 00:32:13,440
This is not a kingdom that struggles and overcomes.

496
00:32:13,440 --> 00:32:14,660
It outlasts.

497
00:32:14,660 --> 00:32:15,500
It endures.

498
00:32:15,500 --> 00:32:17,620
And it endures with patience and joy.

499
00:32:17,620 --> 00:32:19,180
That's what Paul's telling us.

500
00:32:19,180 --> 00:32:22,680
This kingdom of God you're setting up is just going to make it through.

501
00:32:22,880 --> 00:32:27,080
But it's not gritting its teeth and ducking down, and I'm going to make it no matter what.

502
00:32:27,080 --> 00:32:28,700
It's standing up.

503
00:32:28,700 --> 00:32:29,960
It's sharing the command.

504
00:32:29,960 --> 00:32:33,560
And it's with joy spreading the kingdom of God.

505
00:32:33,560 --> 00:32:36,220
Because it's supposed to be, in verse 10, bearing fruit.

506
00:32:36,220 --> 00:32:43,200
We're supposed to have joy giving thanks to the Father who has qualified us to share in the inheritance of the saints and light.

507
00:32:43,200 --> 00:32:47,860
He's delivered us from the domain of darkness and transferred us to this kingdom of his beloved Son,

508
00:32:47,860 --> 00:32:51,260
in whom we have the redemption and the forgiveness of sins.

509
00:32:52,880 --> 00:32:56,560
So, the picture we get in John is of a vine, right?

510
00:32:56,560 --> 00:32:58,280
The kingdom of heaven is a vine.

511
00:32:58,280 --> 00:32:58,700
It grows.

512
00:32:58,700 --> 00:33:02,860
It plants more fruit, which grows, which grows more vines.

513
00:33:02,860 --> 00:33:08,480
And if a branch isn't bearing fruit, it's chopped off, but another one grows, right?

514
00:33:08,480 --> 00:33:12,900
So, while we don't see it now, because it's not visible, it's not of this world,

515
00:33:12,900 --> 00:33:15,560
it's not wiping out the bad guys, right?

516
00:33:15,560 --> 00:33:17,860
It is constantly growing.

517
00:33:21,100 --> 00:33:26,140
In Corinthians, Paul says it's the body of Christ, which is referenced also in Ephesians, right?

518
00:33:26,140 --> 00:33:27,880
That it's a growing thing.

519
00:33:27,880 --> 00:33:28,980
It's an organic thing.

520
00:33:28,980 --> 00:33:30,080
It grows.

521
00:33:30,080 --> 00:33:35,700
And in Ephesians 2.21, he actually speaks of it as a growing building.

522
00:33:35,700 --> 00:33:41,760
Even when he wants to draw the picture of a temple, because we are now the temple,

523
00:33:41,760 --> 00:33:44,080
Christ will dwell in us.

524
00:33:44,640 --> 00:33:48,220
And if someone wants to see Christ and come to worship him, they'll see him in you, right?

525
00:33:48,220 --> 00:33:48,940
Not in the building.

526
00:33:48,940 --> 00:33:53,260
But even when he wants to talk about the picture of the building, he talks about it as a growing building,

527
00:33:53,260 --> 00:34:00,080
because every understanding that the early church had of the kingdom of heaven was that it is nascently planted now when Christ came.

528
00:34:00,080 --> 00:34:06,760
And he planted the church, and it's growing, and it's growing, and it's bearing fruit, and that fruit will grow and bear fruit, right?

529
00:34:07,480 --> 00:34:08,940
That's how the kingdom of God works.

530
00:34:08,940 --> 00:34:12,240
It spreads and grows, and you are a part of it.

531
00:34:12,240 --> 00:34:15,060
It's already seen, but it's not fully realized.

532
00:34:15,060 --> 00:34:18,940
However, we know that, verse 10,

533
00:34:19,480 --> 00:34:26,380
He was made known to us the mystery of his will according to his purpose, which is set forth in Christ as a plan for the fullness of time,

534
00:34:26,380 --> 00:34:30,500
where he will unite all things in him, things in heaven and things on earth.

535
00:34:30,500 --> 00:34:35,860
This kingdom of heaven on earth will be fully realized in the fullness of time.

536
00:34:35,860 --> 00:34:41,620
Ephesians is a letter that explains how that works in practical terms to the people that need to know how to join into it.

537
00:34:41,620 --> 00:34:43,980
Thank goodness, because that's us, right?

538
00:34:45,660 --> 00:34:50,080
So in closing, God plans to reveal his glory through those who are faithful in him.

539
00:34:50,080 --> 00:34:51,080
That's what the letter tells us.

540
00:34:51,080 --> 00:34:53,020
This letter is written to those who are faithful in him.

541
00:34:53,020 --> 00:34:56,160
His kingdom come, his will be done.

542
00:34:56,160 --> 00:35:01,060
God plans to reveal his glory then through you when you're faithful, through your life.

543
00:35:01,060 --> 00:35:06,960
He's chosen us to do this, and he's chosen to do this in a very difficult way because we are inconstant.

544
00:35:06,960 --> 00:35:09,500
We're maybe not as faithful as we want to be.

545
00:35:09,500 --> 00:35:15,400
He's choosing to act with people who are rebellious and who fall away from him and aren't always fruitful.

546
00:35:15,660 --> 00:35:20,180
But he's always there to guard us and to help us grow.

547
00:35:20,180 --> 00:35:29,080
In evaluating how he makes use of our lives, how he invests our life with his will and his purpose and how we commit our lives to him,

548
00:35:29,080 --> 00:35:31,940
we tend to focus on our will, what we will do.

549
00:35:31,940 --> 00:35:34,520
We want to make that second half of this letter happen.

550
00:35:34,520 --> 00:35:37,900
We want to talk about our free will.

551
00:35:37,900 --> 00:35:41,000
We have the option to do this or not, but we've chosen to, some people.

552
00:35:41,700 --> 00:35:46,260
But it's imperative that we focus not on free will, but on his free grace.

553
00:35:46,260 --> 00:35:52,120
Because his grace is over and over what allows us to come back to him and invites us to come back to him and take part in his plan

554
00:35:52,120 --> 00:35:57,220
so that our lives can express his glory in this chaotic and fallen world around us that we are a part of.

555
00:35:59,220 --> 00:36:05,660
And as we come back again and again, asking forgiveness for our faithfulness, our selfishness, our pride.

556
00:36:05,660 --> 00:36:08,860
He will accept us.

557
00:36:08,860 --> 00:36:10,340
We'll be accepted by his grace.

558
00:36:10,340 --> 00:36:16,100
When we humbly accept his grace, which he freely gives us in the character of Christ, we'll grow into the body of Christ.

559
00:36:16,540 --> 00:36:26,380
And the kingdom of God will grow in heaven until, as in verse 10, in the fullness of time, Christ will unite all things in him, in heaven and things on earth.

560
00:36:26,380 --> 00:36:29,660
So this is why we're studying Ephesians for the next five weeks.

561
00:36:29,660 --> 00:36:32,880
Because we want to know how that practically happens in our lives.

562
00:36:32,880 --> 00:36:36,560
And I appreciate all you coming here today.

563
00:36:36,560 --> 00:36:40,180
I appreciate that you're going to read the letter to yourselves this week.

564
00:36:41,380 --> 00:36:43,300
And see you again next week, okay?

565
00:36:43,300 --> 00:36:44,720
Let's close in prayer.

566
00:36:44,720 --> 00:36:51,500
Father God, I thank you so much for the people that have come here to gather in your church.

567
00:36:51,500 --> 00:36:54,980
In the hopes of growing the character of Christ into the body of Christ.

568
00:36:54,980 --> 00:36:56,280
That we will yield to you.

569
00:36:56,280 --> 00:36:58,920
We will accept your grace in the small things.

570
00:36:58,920 --> 00:37:06,420
That we will diminish our own wills so that you can become greater in our lives and into the lives of the people around us.

571
00:37:06,420 --> 00:37:09,940
Pray that you would show us in small ways how to make that happen this week.

572
00:37:09,980 --> 00:37:15,360
And give us moments when, painful though it may be, we can release the pride and our own desires.

573
00:37:15,360 --> 00:37:21,140
And have a moment where we overflow your grace to the world around us.

574
00:37:21,140 --> 00:37:24,720
Overflow your forgiveness, specifically, to the world around us.

575
00:37:24,720 --> 00:37:26,800
Thank you, in Jesus' name, amen.
